FEATURES IMPLEMENTED
=============================================================================

FEATURE 1: Hardware Validation
-----------
Purpose: Ensure hole sizes match hardware specifications
Location: static/js/designer.js lines 736-927

Key Components:
- Automatic validation on hardware selection
- ±1mm tolerance checking
- Hardware size mismatch warning modal
- Override option with safety notices
- Graceful error handling

API Integration:
- GET /api/herrajes/{id} - Fetch hardware specs for validation

User Experience:
1. User selects hardware from dropdown
2. System validates hole size vs. hardware requirement
3. If compatible: Details modal shows automatically
4. If incompatible: Warning modal appears
5. User can cancel or override with confirmation

FEATURE 2: Hardware Details Modal
-----------
Purpose: Display comprehensive hardware information
Location: static/js/designer.js lines 829-1045

Information Displayed:
- Hardware code and name
- Product image (if available)
- Full description
- Specifications (hole size, category, material, max load, etc.)
- Glass thickness range
- Hole pattern type
- Countersink information (if applicable)
- Installation type
- Safety notes

Technical Details:
- Responsive design (600px max-width)
- Scrollable content for mobile
- Z-index: 5000 (stays above other elements)
- Async loading with error handling
- Professional styling with color-coded sections

FEATURE 3: Bill of Materials Generation
-----------
Purpose: Generate complete project specifications for fabrication
Location: static/js/designer.js lines 2537-2798
          templates/designer.html (BOM button)

BOM Sections:
1. Glass Specifications
   - Dimensions and area
   - Thickness and type
   - CPB (polished edge) status
   - Painted areas information

2. Hardware Components
   - Hardware code, name, category
   - Material and finish
   - Quantity (auto-calculated)
   - Hole size and load capacity

3. Holes Summary
   - Count by type (circle, taladro, avellanado, rectangle, clip)
   - Visual cards for each type

4. Summary Statistics
   - Total holes
   - Total hardware items
   - Total glass area

Export Functionality:
- JSON export: `bom-[timestamp].json`
- Contains complete BOM data structure
- Ready for external software integration

